# MongoDB Queries

## 1. Create / Select Database

use Students

## 2. Create Collection

db.createCollection("students")

## 3. Insert Student Records

db.students.insertMany([
  {roll:1, name:"Ananya", age:18, marks:86, city:"Lucknow"},
  {roll:2, name:"Rohan", age:19, marks:74, city:"Kanpur"},
  {roll:3, name:"Meera", age:20, marks:93, city:"Agra"},
  {roll:4, name:"Aditya", age:18, marks:68, city:"Varanasi"},
  {roll:5, name:"Kavya", age:19, marks:82, city:"Lucknow"}
])

> The original project contains 50 student records; the complete dataset is included in the project report.

## 4. Display All Students

db.students.find()

## 5. Equal To — `$eq`

Find students whose marks are exactly 88:

db.students.find({marks: {$eq: 88}})

## 6. Greater Than — `$gt`

Find students whose marks are greater than 85:

db.students.find({marks: {$gt: 85}})

## 7. Less Than — `$lt`

Find students whose marks are less than 60:

db.students.find({marks: {$lt: 60}})

## 8. Greater Than or Equal To — `$gte`

Find students whose marks are 90 or above:

db.students.find({marks: {$gte: 90}})

## 9. Less Than or Equal To — `$lte`

Find students whose marks are 70 or below:

db.students.find({marks: {$lte: 70}})

## 10. Update Operation

Update marks of the student with roll number 5:

db.students.updateOne(
  {roll: 5},
  {$set: {marks: 95}}
)

## 11. Delete One Student

Delete the student with roll number 10:

db.students.deleteOne({roll: 10})

## 12. Delete Multiple Students

Delete students having marks below 60:

db.students.deleteMany({
  marks: {$lt: 60}
})

## 13. AND Operation — `$and`

Find students who have marks greater than 80 **and** are 19 years old:

```javascript
db.students.find({
  $and: [
    {marks: {$gt: 80}},
    {age: 19}
  ]
})
```

## 14. OR Operation — `$or`

Find students from Lucknow **or** Kanpur:

```javascript
db.students.find({
  $or: [
    {city: "Lucknow"},
    {city: "Kanpur"}
  ]
})
```

## 15. Sort — Ascending

Sort students from lowest marks to highest:

```javascript
db.students.find().sort({marks: 1})
```

## 16. Sort — Descending

Sort students from highest marks to lowest:

```javascript
db.students.find().sort({marks: -1})
```

## 17. Limit

Display only the first 5 documents:

```javascript
db.students.find().limit(5)
```

